e loki of elbaf  there is shanks and we remember pel and  chaka's fruit which allowed them to take  the shape of animals that resemble the  gods of the egyptian pantheon the jakar  fruit essentially turned chaka into  anubis while the falcon fruit gave pel  the traits of the egyptian gods horus  the jury is still out though on whether  horus could also survive massive  explosions of a giant bomb but anyways  what if these separate influences play  together so nicely because there are  common threats that run through all of  them well it turns out that almost all  of these religions all over the world  were influenced or inspired by  zoroastrianism in case you're wondering  what the heck that is let me give you a  quick rundown of it before we get into  why it's connected to one piece  zoroastrianism is the world's oldest  known monotheistic religion or the first  major religion to teach that there is  only one supreme gods it originates from  persia located in what is now modern-day  iran this faith is based on the  teachings of a super ancient prophet  called zoroaster or as you might have  heard someone called zaratustra and so  some of the defining features of its  belief systems center around the duality  between good and evil and the eternal  battle between the two and these tenets  of zoroastrianism have become so  widespread around the globe that they've  influenced many other faiths throughout  the world including christianity islam  hinduism and many many more  zoroastrianism might also well be the  world's oldest continuously practiced  religions with many people in the world  still adhering to the zoroastrian phase  to this day one famous practitioner that  you might be surprised at was none other  than queen singer freddie mercury for  instance but clearly now that we know  that the galailla company's peopley  lulu's resemblance to freddie mercury  was no mere coincidence and one piece's  connection to zoroastrianism has been  hinted at way way back all along okay  maybe the freddie mercury one is a bit  of a stretch but now that we've covered  the basics of zoroastrianism it's time  to really dig into how it inspired one  piece so much including sun god nika and  zoro zoroastrian teachings say that the  world was once pure and good but was  slowly corrupted by evil forces however  to defeat this evil and return the world  to its ideal state every 1 000 years a  hero is reincarnated or reborn until  finally with the last cycle the hero  finally vanquishes these forces of evil  now this is a very stark simplification  of some very complex theology of course  you can learn more about it if you get  your hands on a copy of the avesta the  sacred text of zoroastrianism but even  that bit of information should scream  one piece to you like everywhere  everywhere one piece is all about  inherited will almost all of the straw  hats and many other characters have  inherited the will of someone close to  them and luffy himself seems to share so  many parallels with the former king of  the pirates goldie roger roger himself  was too early in arriving to love tale  it seems that there is a cosmic calendar  counting down the time towards some  cataclysmic destiny and luffy is the  fated hero to take part in a great  battle that determines the future of the  worst but most recently we're seeing  that luffy appears to be a reincarnation  of swords for joy boy we know very  little about joy boy so far but we do  know that he played a significant role  in the void century which happened  nearly 1 000 years ago somewhat in line  with zoroastrianism cycle of the reborn  hero another important connection to  zoroastrianism comes from zorro himself  i mean zoroastrianism it's possible that  oda got zaro's name from this religion  because most western viewers of course  when thinking of the name zorros think  of the swashbuckling pulp hero zorro  with two r's but despite antonio  bandera's impressive sword-wheeling  skills the rest of the comparison really  falls apart quite quickly in fact we do  know that zoro wasn't actually named  after this other hero and thanks to the  similar name we now have zorro with two  hours to thank for every english reader  having to suffer through the official  translation calling our favorite  swordsman zolo thanks for that i guess  quick bonus fact here if you're  wondering where the roronua part comes  from well that's derived from the real  life pirate francis  i guess i mean you get it  it's the japanese rendering of that  anyways back to zoroastrianism one of  the most important connections to zorro  is his ashura technique today asuras are  known as divine beings within hinduism  and buddhism but their lineage can  actually be tracked all the way back to  zoroastrianism in fact the supreme god  of zoroastrianism is known as ahura  mazda the ahura pronunciation and  spelling shifting to asura as it moved  across different places times and  languages another connection between  zorro and zoroastrianism comes through  his many brushes with death now it's  said that in climatic battle the great  hero of zoroastrian myth will cause the  dead to be reborn and for the souls lost  in the underworld to be purified and  brought back to the lights and so i  really couldn't help but notice that  zoro has been having a really recent  encounter with the grim reaper himself  but until we find out more about what  that situation was all about it's really  hard to speculate if there is a  connection here another connection  between zoroastrianism and one piece has  to do with fire and light luffy has been  shown to have unexplained powers to  conjure fire he's the foretold hero that  will bring the dawn of the world the one  who will shine light again on the world  that has been shrouded in darkness and  it just so happens that fire and light  are crucial symbols in zoroastrianism in  this religion there is a practice to  light an eternal flame within a place of  worship called a fire temple that sounds  pretty cool and so when the ideas and  values from sorrow astronism are passed  from one person down to the next it is  symbolized by a new flame being lit from  the existing one thus an eternal flame  one that endures the flow of time  represents an inherited will not too  dissimilar from the concept of inherited  will within one piece speaking of  inherited will in addition to being a  new joy boy it would seem that luffy is  also related to a figure called the sun  god nika in zoroastrianism fire is used  to represent the gods ashura mazda and  in addition to this there is also a  zoroastrian moral code that follows  three main principles good thoughts or  pendant good words or golf darnique and  good actions or kerdanique the word nik  which can be translated as good true or  chosen just so happens to be where the  persian name nika originates  the name of the sun god nika literally  comes from zoroastrianism so if you  weren't convinced by any other pieces of  evidence so far i'm sure this one will  make you think twice and while we  focused on the zoroastrianism side of  argument hora sensai also dives deep  into norse mythology as well it's of  course the inspiration for both the  giants of elbaf and our red-haired  legend shanks now shanks and luffy are  bound to meet very soon and if you want  to know why this will most likely take  place on elbaf and why luffy must fight  his mentor at some point you really  can't miss out on this video right here
 

